PW water dimer, two molecules stacked 7.5 bohr apart along z, with native SCCS in a periodic
cell (assume_isolated none), the water-neutral preset and the Environ solvent-aware interface
(sccs_solvent_radius 2, sccs_filling_threshold 0.3). The probe of radius 4 bohr fills the gap
between the molecules but not the gaps to the periodic images: Environ 'chain' derivatives of
the filled boundary and of its surface (gradient and Hessian, as Environ need_hessian), the
probe adjoint in the electronic potential, energy and ionic force.

Reference provenance (ecutwfc 75 Ry / ecutrho 300 Ry, the cutoffs of the QE-Environ comparison):
- ABACUS source commit: bf66e1d58 (fix(surchem): use the chain surface of the periodic solvent-aware boundary;
  the executable was built before a message-only history rewrite and reports e40515a45, same tree)
- ABACUS version: v3.11.0-beta10
- executable SHA256: 3c97ec43a21ae82301947b4974dbec14adeb9da38db053345e6c3976b065fac1
- parallel layout: 16 MPI ranks x 1 OpenMP thread
- generated 2026-10-01; two independent check runs passed every comparison.
- sccs_debug 2 reports SCCS_CAVITY SURFACE/Bohr2 365.7 and FILLED_VOLUME/Bohr3 104.8 at
  convergence. The earlier baseline (1a7794b63) took the surface from the spectral gradient of
  the filled boundary, which rings at this low sccs_filling_threshold: surface 410.5 bohr^2,
  E_sol_cav 0.0378 eV higher.
- result.ref is an ABACUS regression baseline, not an external QE/Environ reference; the
  solvent-aware kernel was compared with QE-Environ 3.1.1 on Environ's own solvent-aware test
  system (see the PR description).

Repository harness regeneration command, run from tests/01_PW:
  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 bash ../integrate/Autotest.sh -a /path/to/abacus -n 16 -o 1 -r '^227_PW_SCCS_SA_PERIODIC_WATER2$' -g
